00:53:15.015 --> 00:53:22.444
Jill McNitt-Gray: This is something that's highly regulated in divers, so this is very interesting, because you want to get the most out at the right time.


314
00:53:22.445 --> 00:53:38.305
Manny Azizi: Exactly. The timing of that… so, jumping straight, yeah, you've seen… you can see divers, like, hit the wrong timing, and it just looks super awkward, because they just did not get… get that push from the substrate.


315
00:53:38.565 --> 00:53:45.334
Manny Azizi: But we do have… we have another paper coming out that utilizes our virtual reality system.


316
00:53:45.335 --> 00:53:45.705
Jill McNitt-Gray: Thanks.


317
00:53:45.705 --> 00:53:49.264
Manny Azizi: with a compliant substrate as well.


318
00:53:49.645 --> 00:53:52.775
Manny Azizi: And we were able to recapitulate that,


319
00:53:52.935 --> 00:54:03.615
Manny Azizi: The model stays in contact longer because the takeoff powers and velocities are dampened by reducing the quality of the latch.


